.Dd July 13, 2023
.Dt DUT 1
.Os
.
.Sh NAME
.Nm dut
.Nd disk usage calculator
.
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl cClsbphv
.Op Fl d Ar depth
.Op Fl i Ar indent
.Op Fl n Ar rows
.Op Fl t Ar threads
.Op Ar path...
.
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a configurable, fast disk usage calculator for Linux, capable of
de-duplicating hardlinks.
.
.Pp
If invoked without an argument,
.Nm
will search the current working directory.  Otherwise,
.Nm
will traverse all directories listed in
.Ar path... .
.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.
.It Fl c
Disable colorized output.  This has the same effect as a non-empty
value in the
.Ev NO_COLOR
environmental variable.
.
.It Fl C
Force colorized output.  This overrides the environmental variable
.Ev NO_COLOR .
.
.It Fl l
Count every instance of a hard link.
.
.It Fl b
Show sizes in plain bytes intead of human readable format.
.
.It Fl s
Use size of files instead of size on disk.
.
.It Fl p
Display full path of files in the tree.
.
.It Fl d Ar depth
Limit the
.Ar depth
of the traversed file system in the output.
.
.It Fl i Ar indentation
Specify the number of spaces for each level of
.Ar indentation .
The default is 2.
.
.It Fl n Ar rows
Specify the number of
.Ar rows
to show.  The default is 10 rows less than the terminal size.
.
.It Fl t Ar threads
Number of
.Ar threads
to use.  The default is the number online processors.  See also
.Xr get_nprocs_conf 3 .
.
.It Fl h
Display a help message.
.
.It Fl v
Display version information.
.
.El
.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
If the
.Ev NO_COLOR
environmental variable has a non-empty value, then the output will not
include any color
.Po
see the
.Fl c
option and also
.Lk https://no-color.org/
.Pc .
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr du 1 ,
.Xr ncdu 1 ,
.Xr dua 1 ,
.Xr pdu 1 ,
.Xr dust 1 ,
.Xr gdu 1
